  {
    "observed": {
      "loops": [
        "## Open loops",
        "",
        "It is <weekday> <local-time> (UTC) now. These are the things still open between you and the people here: always in front of you until they are closed. Open one with `open_loop` when something stays unresolved or someone asks to be reminded (\"remind me about the meeting on Wednesday\"), with a time anchor when it has a time (`at`, or `cron` when it repeats; `autoClose` when the time is the thing itself, like a meeting or a deadline). Use `touch_loop` when one comes up, `update_loop` when it changes, and `close_loop` with the reason once it is resolved or someone says it no longer matters; `reopen_loop` when they say it is not done. `from` says where each came from: only `user` is the people's own word. Past 40, the ones without a time that were mentioned least recently go to memory.",
        "",
        "(none)"
      ],
      "toolResult": [
        "Opened [<loop:1>] Team meeting (from user; next <weekday> <local-time> (UTC), repeats `0 18 * * 3`)"
